The code statements that lead to the bug are:
mci->pvt_info = kzalloc(sz_pvt, GFP_KERNEL);
if (!mci->pvt_info)
    goto error;
...
mci->dev.release = mci_release;
device_initialize(&mci->dev);
Reason:
The device initialization (setting the release function and calling device_initialize()) happens *after* the allocation of mci->pvt_info. If that allocation fails, the error path calls put_device() (via _edac_mc_free) on an uninitialized device, causing a warning or crash because the kobject underlying the device is not yet ready.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
mci->dev.release = mci_release;
device_initialize(&mci->dev);
...
mci->pvt_info = kzalloc(sz_pvt, GFP_KERNEL);
if (!mci->pvt_info)
    goto error;
Reason:
By moving the device initialization before the allocation of pvt_info, the device is fully initialized before any potential failure point. Thus, if the allocation fails, the error path can safely call put_device() on a properly initialized device, avoiding the undefined behavior.

